--TEST--
a call outside the places a `[[restrict]]` entry allows is published as `E0664` with where it is allowed in the message, and a related location at the entry's line in `package.toml`, `rule:packaging/a-restriction-limits-where-a-declaration-is-used`
--FILE--
<?nvs
autoload 'App' from './app';

echo App\Secret\Vault::open(), "\n";
--FILE app/Secret/Vault.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace App\Secret;

final class Vault
{
    public static function open(): string
    {
        return "open";
    }
}
--FILE package.toml--
[[restrict]]
use = 'App\Secret\Vault::open'
allow = ['App\Allowed']
note = 'Use `App\Allowed\Door::open`.'
--REQUEST--
diagnostics
--EXPECT--
4:6-4:30 error E0664 `App\Secret\Vault::open` cannot be used here. It is allowed only in `App\Allowed`. Use `App\Allowed\Door::open`.
  related package.toml:2:7 the restriction
